 ### SnowPakTool Desktop UI
 
-A compiled **slot-based upgrade selection draft** is available as `UpgradeDistributionPlanner.Generate(input, seed, options)`. It selects new rewards from the supplied eligible full catalog while retaining each pickup's original type and fixed metal detectors. Truck-specific slots prefer unused upgrades compatible with local obtainable trucks; shared slots draw from all eligible shared parts of that type, with an extra foreign preference in the first region. Fallbacks broaden the same-type pool before reuse. There is no locality quota or whole-plan optimizer, and original reward IDs/counts need not be retained. It performs no file writes and is not connected to the Upgrades UI yet; verified compatibility/composite tire IDs and effective truck/contract-reward homes must be supplied by a future catalog adapter. See [the planner draft and input contract](upgrade-distribution-draft.md).
+A **slot-based upgrade preview trial** is available in **Randomizer → Upgrades**. Randomize upgrades builds the full component catalog from the workspace, resolves composite tire IDs, uses current obtainable map-truck previews plus direct garage/contract rewards, and saves a preview under `workspace/upgrade-randomization/draft.json`. Region progression must be finalized. Only owned regions are generated; replacement eligibility uses enabled trucks and explicit tire-pack ownership. Each pickup retains its original type, and metal detectors stay fixed. Truck-specific slots prefer unused local-compatible parts; shared slots use all eligible shared parts without a purchase-only restriction, with an extra foreign preference in the first region. Fallbacks broaden the same-type pool before reuse. Stock/default-only and objective-locked replacements are excluded conservatively. There is no locality quota. See [the planner and input contract](upgrade-distribution-draft.md).
 
 **Editors → Addons** provides a read-only addon/upgrade catalog using Cargo's main table, description and source-properties layout. Reload runs in the background. Shared column sorting/filtering covers names, type/category, IDs and ID scope, socket/component family, content, price, rank, exploration flag and map reward references. Selecting an item lists each level SSO's map, zone and reward index, plus XML properties and their source files. Explicit file parents are followed; templates remain visible source data without expansion, and full truck compatibility is not inferred. Tire names are local to their wheel family; unresolved map reward IDs remain clearly marked. This does not stage or edit game data. See [the upgrade investigation](upgrade-map-investigation.md) for the confirmed map-zone → level-settings → part-definition relationship and replacement limits.
 
-**Randomizer → Upgrades** prepares the upgrade workflow with one full-width rule pane, matching Truck randomization's add/edit/remove glyphs, automatically saved notes, Randomize / Stage changes buttons, detailed-log toggle and message area. Rules start empty and save separately from truck rules; an intentionally empty list remains empty. **Randomizer → Map upgrades** matches Map trucks' region tiles, map-folder Browse / Reload controls, region selection buttons, reset/staging controls, sortable/filterable table and resizable details split. Region tiles load from workspace metadata. Upgrade placement reading, replacement, randomization, reset and staging are not implemented yet; their action buttons remain disabled. Browse selects a folder and Reload refreshes workspace region metadata; neither scans upgrade placements or writes game files. Redistribution rules will be defined separately.
+**Randomizer → Upgrades** uses one rule pane with matching add/edit/remove glyphs, automatically saved notes, a run button, default-hidden detailed logs and region completion messages. Fresh rule files receive the implemented rule notes; existing custom notes and intentional empty lists remain intact. Editing rule prose does not change the algorithm. Logs report seed/counts without revealing replacement identities. **Randomizer → Map upgrades** reads original level-SSO pickup settings and shows original/preview names, types, compatible truck IDs, source zone and change state. Region tiles, column sorting/filtering and details match Map trucks. Reset selected covers all visible filtered rows, reset regions covers selected regions independently of column filters, and reset all covers the loaded catalog. These actions remove preview assignments only. Reload refreshes sources; changed truck/ownership/progression inputs mark saved previews stale for explicit rerandomization. The source row identifies initial-PAK level settings; map-folder selection stays in Map trucks. **Upgrade Stage/Apply is disabled in this trial.** No XML, SSO, map archive or installed game file is changed by randomizing/resetting upgrades; trial previews are not added to Start's staged changes.
 
 **Start → PAK** groups truck XML changes into one brief row per truck and state, using the localized truck name. The summary shows up to three readable field/value changes (for example fuel capacity, price, unlock rank, engine or winch compatibility), followed by a count of further changes. Hover for every original field, before/after value and source path. Pending and applied summaries retain their distinct colors. Rank XP, shared engine/winch definitions, addon files and other general edits remain separate entries. Grouping affects display only; Apply and pending counts still use the full underlying edit list.
 
